VibeTracks License

Copyright (c) 2026 VibeTracks contributors

VibeTracks is a lab for authoring game assets as specs — songs compiled to audio,
characters compiled to spritesheets. This license covers the parts of this
repository that the VibeTracks authors wrote, and defers to third parties for the
parts they wrote.

1. The software and the specs

   The source code, and the JSON specs and compositions authored in this
   repository, are provided freely. You may use, copy, modify, and distribute
   them, and use whatever you create with them — rendered audio, spritesheets,
   your own specs — for any purpose, commercial or not, without royalty.

   If you build something out of this (a tool, a game, a derivative), please give
   reasonable credit to VibeTracks, and retain this notice in copies of the source.

2. Bundled artwork and other third-party assets — their licenses come first

   This repository bundles and composes artwork created by other people (for
   example, the Liberated Pixel Cup sprite layers under sprites/*/assets/). Those
   assets are NOT covered by Section 1. They remain under their creators' own
   licenses, which take precedence and must be honored first.

   Each such asset's author, license, and source are recorded alongside it — see
   the CREDITS files (e.g. sprites/<cast>/CREDITS.csv). Some of those licenses
   require attribution and/or impose share-alike (copyleft) terms on works that
   include the art. When you distribute anything that incorporates a bundled asset,
   you must comply with that asset's license — attribution and all — before the
   permissions in Section 1 apply to the rest.

   In short: credit the artists, honor their terms, then freely use what is yours.

3. No warranty

   The software and assets are provided "as is", without warranty of any kind,
   express or implied. In no event shall the authors be liable for any claim,
   damages, or other liability arising from their use.
